# Line endings
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout and prints a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning for every file it
# touches. The files in this project use LF, so that warning appeared on every
# single publish. It was harmless, but it buried the output that actually
# matters.
#
# Declaring the endings here settles it: the repository stores LF and the
# working copy keeps LF, so Git has nothing to convert and nothing to warn
# about. Every editor on Windows worth using (Notepad included, since Windows
# 10) reads LF files correctly.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted, or they corrupt.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
